# Every variable below (except the two at the bottom) lives in the personal
# env-vault, project "project-x" — that's the actual source of truth for
# local dev, CI, and the deployed site. `pnpm dev`/`pnpm start` already wrap
# `envvault run project-x -- ...`, so nothing here needs a real value for
# this repo to run: this file exists to document what exists and why, and as
# a fallback path (fill in `.env.local` yourself instead) on a machine that
# doesn't have vault access.
#
# One-time vault setup on a new machine:
#   curl -fsS https://env-vault-api.alexdev93.workers.dev/install.sh | sh
#   envvault login   # paste the vault URL + your API token
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and holds only what genuinely differs by
# environment and so has no business in a shared vault — see the bottom of
# this file. Do not add a key here "just in case": `dev`/`start` layer
# `.env.local` over the vault with dotenv's `-o` (override), so a key present
# with an empty value replaces a real vault value with nothing.

# --- AI assistant ----------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only. Read exclusively inside the AI modules and never exposed to the
# browser. Do NOT prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Chat model. Default: gemini-3.5-flash-lite — current generation, free tier,
# supports tool calling and streaming. Raise to gemini-3.7-flash for stronger
# reasoning (also free tier, higher paid rate).
AI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Embedding model and output width. 768 keeps the table small; the model also
# supports 1536 and 3072. Changing this requires editing the VECTOR(...) width
# in src/lib/db/schema.sql and re-running `yarn db:migrate` + `yarn ingest`.
AI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=gemini-embedding-001
AI_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=768

# --- Retrieval -------------------------------------------------------------
# Chunks fetched per question, and the minimum cosine similarity to count as
# relevant. Below the threshold a chunk is dropped rather than cited.
#
# 0.66 is measured against this corpus: correct answers score 0.664-0.734 while
# the best off-topic match tops out at 0.633, so the threshold sits in the gap.
# Lowering it makes answers cite content they did not really use.
RAG_TOP_K=5
RAG_MIN_SCORE=0.66

# --- Vector store (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Postgres with pgvector. Neon's free tier is enough for this corpus.
#
# OPTIONAL BY DESIGN: with this unset the assistant still works — it answers
# from the full portfolio context and simply omits source citations. A cold,
# missing or over-quota database degrades citations, never the chat.
DATABASE_URL=

# --- Limits and caching ----------------------------------------------------
# Requests per window per IP, and the window in seconds.
AI_RATE_LIMIT=10
AI_RATE_WINDOW=60

# Cached answer lifetime in seconds. 0 disables caching.
AI_CACHE_TTL=3600

# Input caps and the upstream timeout in milliseconds.
AI_MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH=2000
AI_MAX_HISTORY=20
AI_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# --- Sign-in (Google, via Better Auth) -------------------------------------
# All three are needed together, or none. Missing any of them disables sign-in
# and nothing else: the blog still reads perfectly, because reading never
# requires a session. Comment forms are replaced with a note, and /api/auth/*
# returns 503 while logging exactly which variable is absent.
#
# Server-only, every one of them. There is no NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable in this
# feature at all — the OAuth redirect is built on the server.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET signs the session cookie. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
#
# From the Google Cloud console: APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID
# (Web application). Free. Add BOTH redirect URIs:
#   https://<your-site>/api/auth/callback/google
#   http://localhost:3001/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- LinkedIn (optional; for cross-posting a published blog post) ---------
# Both needed together, or neither: missing either just disables the
# "share to LinkedIn" step, nothing else. From a LinkedIn developer app
# (linkedin.com/developers/apps) with the "Share on LinkedIn" and "Sign In
# with LinkedIn using OpenID Connect" products added — both self-service,
# free, no LinkedIn review required. Add BOTH redirect URIs on the app:
#   https://<your-site>/api/auth/callback/linkedin
#   http://localhost:3001/api/auth/callback/linkedin
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Blob storage (optional; for a post's cover image) ----------------------
# Missing this just disables cover images: a post can still publish and share
# to LinkedIn, it just does so as a plain link with no thumbnail. Enable Blob
# storage for this project in the Vercel dashboard (Storage tab -> Create
# Database -> Blob) -- free tier, no other setup. Its dashboard hands you
# three values (this one plus the two below) — put all three in the vault,
# not just this one.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
BLOB_STORE_ID=
BLOB_WEBHOOK_PUBLIC_KEY=

# --- Administrators --------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated email addresses allowed into /admin. Compared exactly, after
# trimming and lower-casing, and the address must be verified by its provider.
#
# FAILS CLOSED: unset or empty means nobody is an administrator, including the
# owner. That is deliberate — a deployment that forgets this variable locks the
# admin panel rather than opening it.
#
# Deliberately not a database column. Administrator rights are configuration,
# so no SQL write path can grant them; the database only ever stores the
# opposite capability, in blocked_users.
ADMIN_EMAILS=

# --- Blog (all optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these has a working default; they exist for tuning, not setup.
# Not in the vault — there's nothing to configure unless you want a non-default.
BLOG_PAGE_SIZE=10
BLOG_REVALIDATE_SECONDS=300
BLOG_COMMENT_MAX_LENGTH=2000
BLOG_COMMENT_RATE_LIMIT=5
BLOG_COMMENT_RATE_WINDOW=300
BLOG_COMMENT_EDIT_WINDOW_MINUTES=15
#
# `post` publishes comments immediately and lets you hide them afterwards;
# `pre` holds every comment for approval. A comment carrying three or more links
# is held for approval either way — held, not rejected, so a legitimate
# link-heavy reply costs its author a delay rather than their words.
BLOG_COMMENT_MODERATION=post

# --- Site content editor (optional) ----------------------------------------
# Lets /admin/content save changes to the portfolio's text. Saving writes a
# commit to the repository, which triggers a deployment — so the token needs to
# write files, and nothing else.
#
# Create a FINE-GRAINED personal access token at
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#   Repository access: only this repository
#   Permissions:       Contents → Read and write
# Nothing more. A classic token with `repo` scope would reach every repository
# you can see, which this feature has no need for.
#
# Unset, the editor still shows the current content but cannot save.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITHUB_REPO=alexdev93/project-x
# The branch commits land on. Defaults to main.
GITHUB_BRANCH=main

# --- App downloads (private repos) ------------------------------------------
# Lets the "Apps" section on /projects offer a direct APK download for an app
# whose repo is private (e.g. SpendGuard). A private repo's release assets
# 404 for an anonymous request even with the exact URL, so /api/apps/<slug>/
# download authenticates to GitHub, resolves that app's `releases/latest`,
# and streams the .apk back from this site's own origin — visitors are never
# sent to github.com, and a new tagged release is live on the next click with
# no redeploy here.
#
# Create a FINE-GRAINED personal access token at
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#   Repository access: only the app repo(s) this should be able to read
#   Permissions:       Contents → Read-only
# One token covers every private app repo it's granted access to.
#
# Unset, the download button still renders (it's driven by the app's own
# downloadUrl in content) but every click 503s — check the server log.
APPS_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Contact form (Gmail SMTP) ---------------------------------------------
# EMAIL_PASS must be a Google App Password, not your account password.
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
EMAIL_USER=
EMAIL_PASS=

# --- Analytics (PostHog, optional) ------------------------------------------
# Page views, clicks (autocapture) and custom events, with country and
# device/browser breakdowns computed by PostHog itself — nothing to build for
# those two. Free for up to 1M events/month, no server to host.
#
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_ on purpose: a PostHog project token can only write
# events into one project, never read them back out, so there is nothing
# secret about it — same as a Google Analytics measurement ID.
#
# Unset, analytics is simply off: PostHogProvider renders nothing and nothing
# else changes. Sign up free at https://posthog.com, create a project, and
# copy its token from Project Settings — or run `npx @posthog/wizard@latest`,
# which prints both variables below already filled in.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
# Defaults to PostHog's US cloud. Use https://eu.i.posthog.com if your project
# is on the EU region (chosen at signup, shown in Project Settings).
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# --- Site -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute base URL, used for canonical URLs, sitemap and Open Graph tags.
# The vault holds the real production value (https://alemayehu.vercel.app,
# with the scheme — a bare domain breaks `new URL()` in src/lib/site.ts).
# No line for it here: see .env.local below for why local dev needs a
# different value than the one the vault supplies.

# =============================================================================
# Everything below this line is NOT in the vault — copy just these two lines
# into your own `.env.local`, nothing else. They're genuinely per-environment
# (a local port, a matching localhost URL) rather than shared config, and
# `dev`/`start` load `.env.local` with dotenv's `-o` (override) precisely so
# these two beat whatever the vault says. Leave PORT unset for Next's own
# default (3000).
# =============================================================================
PORT=3001
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3001
